# Copy to .env.local for local work; set the same names in Vercel for production (docs/operations/DEPLOY.md).
# Names only: never commit a real value. `npm run check:env` checks a file against lib/env and prints what is on.
# The first group is all the app needs to run. Every other group is optional: leave its lines commented and the
# app uses the fallback named in its heading. `npm run check:env -- <file> --production` requires the sign-in
# email, Turnstile and every provider for a deploy. lib/env rejects an empty value, so comment a line out
# rather than leaving it blank.

# ===== Required =====

# Postgres with the pgvector extension (Neon or any other). Production uses its own database, never the dev one.
DATABASE_URL=
# Tests and the gate never use DATABASE_URL: they run on the local Postgres from docker-compose.yml.
# Optional override of that base (must be a local host):
# TEST_DATABASE_BASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5437/understudy

# Random string, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. Different per environment.
AUTH_SECRET=
# Anthropic key: drafts every reply and decides when Jev is off.
CLAUDE_SECRET_KEY=

# ===== Optional: without it, the install still runs =====

# --- Origin (required in production) ---
# Public origin of the app, no trailing slash: http://localhost:3000 locally, https://<domain> in production.
# AUTH_URL=

# --- Jev (TypeSafe) — without it: Claude makes the reply decisions alone ---
# TYPESAFE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- llm-gateway — without it: every call goes straight to Claude and Jev ---
# The gateway's origin with no /v1, and the default key. Also switch on `gateway.generate.enabled` and/or
# `gateway.decide.enabled` in the config table (both false until then). A creator with a gateway tenant of their own sets
# their `gateway.key_env` row to the name of another variable that holds their key.
# GATEWAY_URL=
# GATEWAY_KEY=

# --- Voyage — without it: retrieval is Postgres full-text search whatever retrieval.strategy says ---
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=

# --- Stripe — without it: a demo wallet on the welcome credit, top-ups are off, /api/webhooks/stripe is a 404 ---
# Test-mode secret key (sk_test_...) and the signing secret (whsec_...) of the webhook endpoint
# https://<domain>/api/webhooks/stripe. Locally, `stripe listen` prints its own whsec_. Both or neither.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Pusher Channels — without it: no realtime events, the browser polls ---
# All four server keys, or none.
# PUSHER_APP_ID=
# PUSHER_KEY=
# PUSHER_SECRET=
# PUSHER_CLUSTER=
# Browser copies of PUSHER_KEY and PUSHER_CLUSTER; they must hold the same values.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PUSHER_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PUSHER_CLUSTER=

# --- Sign-in email via Resend — without it: the sign-in link is printed to the server console (never in production) ---
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# Sender on a domain verified in Resend, e.g. Juno <hello@example.com>.
# EMAIL_FROM=

# --- Cloudflare Turnstile — without it: no human check outside production (production refuses to sign anyone in) ---
# The site key is public (sent to the browser); the production hostname must be added to the widget. Both or neither.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Vercel Cron — without it: the sweep route answers 401 (production only; read by /api/cron/sweep, not by lib/env) ---
# Random string. Vercel sends it as `Authorization: Bearer <value>`.
# CRON_SECRET=

# --- Seed and demo seats — without them: no shared creator or admin seats ---
# Creator seat and comma-separated admin seats, created by `npm run db:seed`.
# SEED_CREATOR_EMAIL=
# SEED_ADMIN_EMAILS=
# Shared password for those seats; without it the seats cannot sign in.
# DEMO_SEAT_PASSWORD=

# --- Leak check — without these: the gate step `leak` skips what they would check ---
# Absolute path of a private raw scrape (one folder per handle). When set, the gate fails if any of its
# text or handles appears in the tree.
# LEAK_CHECK_RAW=~/.understudy/<handle>/raw   (a leading ~/ is the home directory)
# A private text file of names that must never appear in a tracked file or path: one term per line, `#` comments,
# terms of 3+ characters. Matched case-insensitively on word boundaries; a space or hyphen inside a term is optional.
# A hit prints file:line and the match's length, never the term. `npm run persona:leak -- --require` fails (exit 2)
# when this or LEAK_CHECK_RAW is unset or empty.
# LEAK_CHECK_NAMES=~/.understudy/names.txt
